WEBVTT

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:04.020
A client from the Underworld?

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.030
You can travel from the Underworld 
to the mundane world?

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.570
It's not common.

00:00:10.690 --> 00:00:13.280
It's a lot of work for a yokai 
to leave the Underworld.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:13.280
That's the opposite of what we usually do.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.280
It's a lot of work for a yokai 
to leave the Underworld.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.040
But this client is going to the trouble 
of coming to the mundane world.

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:22.540
Why's that, Abeno-san?

00:01:55.550 --> 00:02:00.550
<b>Mystery 3 "Greetings"</b>

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.560
Observing a mundane world school, huh?

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.240
Observing the school is essential 
to improving the standards

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:14.680
of the educational environment of the 
Underworld, and so on and so forth.

00:02:14.680 --> 00:02:16.150
You summarized that too briefly!

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:19.220
She'll be observing the 
school for three days.

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:22.280
She's asked us to accompany 
her during that time.

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:26.680
<i>Since Abeno-san has issues communicating, 
I should be more helpful than usual</i>

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:28.780
<i>at showing someone around the school.</i>

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:31.540
<i>I'll be the perfect guide.</i>

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:33.040
Hey, Ashiya.

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.700
Ashiyan, are you heading home?

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.600
Yeah, Saga, Fusshi.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.980
Fusshi and I were just talking...

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:42.050
Tomorrow's Saturday. Wanna 
go bowling in the afternoon?

00:02:42.700 --> 00:02:44.310
Sounds fun! Oh...

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.810
Are you busy?

00:02:46.810 --> 00:02:48.100
No, but...

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.020
<i>When is the client coming?</i>

00:02:52.020 --> 00:02:54.620
<i>Surely not tomorrow.</i>

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:56.070
I'm free.

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.720
Great! It's decided.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.860
We finally get to bowl again.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.260
Go easy on us.

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:04.700
Modoribashi High School

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:08.500
Morning, Ashiyan.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.460
Good morning, Fusshi.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:12.520
Saturday sure was fun.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:15.060
I can't believe Saga wanted 
to play eight games.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.020
I was so sore, I slept all day on Sunday.

00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.470
Me, too.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:22.220
Morning.

00:03:22.220 --> 00:03:24.090
Good morning, Fushimi-kun, Ashiya-kun.

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:26.420
Good morning, Fusshi, Ashiya.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:28.100
Morning, Saga.

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.100
Good morning...

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:31.730
Ashiya?

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.780
<i>I'll just ignore her!</i>

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:36.440
So you're Ashiya-dono.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.680
My name is Egen.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.240
I'm here to observe your school.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:46.240
<i>Observe?</i>

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.280
Oh, from last week—

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.250
Last week?

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.750
<i>I said that out loud!</i>

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:57.500
I haven't seen you since last 
Friday! Right, Abeno-san?

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.510
Isn't that true for everyone, 
since it's Monday?

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:03.060
Memorizing your textbook, huh?

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:06.860
We do have a test coming up.
 I'd better study, too.

00:04:06.860 --> 00:04:08.720
Right, Abeno-san?

00:04:09.920 --> 00:04:13.460
<i>So this yokai is the client 
Abeno-san mentioned last week.</i>

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:17.600
<i>A yokai who came from the Underworld 
to observe the mundane world.</i>

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.530
<i>I think he said it was for three days.</i>

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.780
Hey, what are you staring at?

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.800
Oh, look! A bug!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.420
<i>Uh-oh... Abeno-san is really angry.</i>

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.290
<i>I need to do something.</i>

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:33.660
Abeno-dono, Ashiya-dono.

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:40.080
My being here may interfere 
with your studies.

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:43.980
However, I was finally granted this 
valuable opportunity to observe.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.740
I shall continue my observation.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.660
I must learn as much as 
possible before I depart.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:56.190
Creating a school where everyone 
can study is my long-held dream.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:59.440
<i>She came so she can establish a school?</i>

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:05.200
For all those who placed their hopes 
in me, I will make it a reality!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.360
<i>All right! I'll make up for 
the mistake I made earlier</i>

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:13.700
<i>by using my communication skills to 
be the perfect guide for Egen-san.</i>

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:18.240
Good morning.

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:19.960
Class officer, lead the class.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:28.260
At the center of atoms and protons are 
nuclei composed of protons and neutrons,

00:05:28.260 --> 00:05:33.320
with electrons circling 
around them on fixed orbits.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:35.980
The types of chemical bonds 
these form are ionic bonds,

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:40.540
covalent bonds, metallic 
bonds, and hydrogen bonds.

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.360
Incredible!

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:42.860
<i>Is science class really that amazing?</i>

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.860
The difference between these are...

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:47.640
Everyone studying here can read and write.

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:50.100
Incredible!

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.120
They all have matching study materials, too.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:57.920
Sir, what does "nuckle" refer to?

00:05:57.920 --> 00:06:00.280
It's not a fist, right?

00:06:00.280 --> 00:06:02.940
That's NaCl. It's salt.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:03.880
Salt?!

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.060
And there are even instructors 
well-versed in their fields.

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.520
How I envy this educational environment!

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:17.520
But how much will it cost to create 
a similar facility in the Underworld?

00:06:17.900 --> 00:06:25.280
<i>So having literacy, textbooks, 
and teachers is enviably amazing to her.</i>

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:27.380
Ashiya-kun.

00:06:27.380 --> 00:06:29.910
Why are you staring at the ceiling?

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:32.160
<i>I was staring at her again!</i>

00:06:32.160 --> 00:06:34.540
What are you spacing out for, Ashiya?

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.800
You were looking off in random 
directions this morning, too.

00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:40.540
Focus on your textbook, please.

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.540
Sorry...

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:45.300
<i>All right, he's asleep! Lucky me!</i>

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:57.430
The savage beast Ashiya-kun ran 
into while running his errand...

00:06:57.760 --> 00:06:59.980
That was definitely the Justice, wasn't it?

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:02.580
You didn't notice?

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:08.280
Not many yokai would fearlessly 
travel to the Birdcage.

00:07:09.360 --> 00:07:12.950
And given that it looked 
like a savage beast...

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:18.950
I was too furious to notice then, 
but now that you mention it...

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.040
I didn't think anything of significance

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:23.760
would happen since he was 
just delivering a document.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.460
I can't believe he encountered the Justice.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:31.970
If the Executive hears about 
Ashiya-kun through this incident...

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:37.930
It may not be a bad idea 
to be careful, Itsuki.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.700
This will be on the test.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:45.320
Make sure you remember it.

00:07:45.320 --> 00:07:48.440
Next, page 87.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:52.200
<i>"Dear Abeno-san, I'm sorry about earlier.</i>

00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:56.380
<i>I promise I'll show Egen-san 
around the school.</i>

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:58.120
<i>You can count on me."</i>

00:07:58.120 --> 00:07:59.700
<i>That should do it.</i>

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.640
<i>He's still angry?!</i>

00:08:06.640 --> 00:08:09.840
<i>I'll admit accidentally speaking 
to Egen-san was a mistake,</i>

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:12.220
<i>but he doesn't need to be </i>that<i> angry!</i>

00:08:12.220 --> 00:08:15.220
I got the last croquette roll!

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.040
You can have it, Saga.

00:08:17.040 --> 00:08:19.340
Really? Thanks.

00:08:19.340 --> 00:08:20.220
Huh?

00:08:21.340 --> 00:08:22.540
Where's Abeno?

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:26.230
He was here when we said 
we were going to the store.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:27.540
Yeah...

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:29.980
<i>Egen-san's missing, too.</i>

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:34.360
Abeno-dono, could you explain this as well?

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.380
There's something called a print shop.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.940
A print shop...

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:41.640
<i>Stare...</i>

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.360
Um... What are you doing out here?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:45.870
You could've said something.

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.700
You didn't come back even 
after I finished lunch.

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.340
You've been up here talking to Egen-san, huh?

00:08:52.340 --> 00:08:54.880
You should've invited me, too.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.000
I can help you show her around the school.

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.140
Excuse me, Ashiya-dono.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.080
Yes?

00:09:01.780 --> 00:09:05.890
Why are you wearing different clothes now?

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:10.000
This? Because I have PE next period.

00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:13.660
I came to get you for that, Abeno-san.

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:18.960
PE? What kind of class is PE?

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.040
It's the most fun out of all the classes.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:23.840
The most fun?

00:09:23.840 --> 00:09:26.720
You should offer PE at 
Underworld schools, too.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.820
I look forward to observing this class.

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.050
Also... I have another question.

00:09:33.050 --> 00:09:34.800
Ask me anything!

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:39.760
Your employee is human, as well.

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.810
That has nothing to do with 
your observational visit.

00:09:48.860 --> 00:09:50.860
Abeno-san?

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.070
Abenon, Abenon.

00:09:55.070 --> 00:09:57.450
You didn't skip today.

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.450
Hey, Abenon.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.740
Abenon.

00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:04.940
Have I offended Abeno-dono?

00:10:04.940 --> 00:10:07.580
I'm glad he didn't cancel my visit.

00:10:08.180 --> 00:10:13.420
Now then, next is this PE that Ashiya-dono 
mentioned, the most fun of all classes.

00:10:13.420 --> 00:10:16.970
I must thoroughly study 
and observe this class.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:20.920
Abeno-san, I guess we're on opposite teams.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:25.540
Ashiya, we're on the same team.

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:27.100
Yeah.

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.600
Abenon, we're on the same team.

00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.600
What's his problem?

00:10:39.620 --> 00:10:41.400
Is this studying?

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.700
It just looks like they're playing.

00:10:46.500 --> 00:10:50.120
This won't be necessary for 
the Underworld's schools.

00:10:50.120 --> 00:10:51.660
Nice, Ashiya!

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:53.130
Yes!

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:58.480
Hey, cut it out!

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:11.400
"PE involves studying while 
using both your mind and body.

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.600
It is a fun kind of study. PE is necessary."

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:18.320
So this is another way to study.

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.900
Fushimi and Abeno, keep running!

00:11:21.640 --> 00:11:23.530
Egen-san, I'm sorry!

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:28.560
I was supposed to help you observe the 
school, but I got caught up playing soccer!

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:32.040
Not at all. It was very informative.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.720
It was?

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:37.760
Since class is over now, we can take 
our time showing you around the school.

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:40.420
That won't be necessary.

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:41.300
Huh?

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.020
Master of the Mononokean, Abeno Haruitsuki,

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:51.140
requesting a portal to the Underworld.

00:11:54.700 --> 00:11:57.690
What? Today's your last day?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:02.120
There were no classes the first day, 
so I was simply shown around the school.

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:06.000
The second day, I observed various 
places around the mundane world

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.830
and watched him exorcise a yokai.

00:12:08.830 --> 00:12:12.060
<i>W-We had work on Saturday?</i>

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.220
Did I skip work?

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:16.080
No, he didn't tell me anything!

00:12:16.080 --> 00:12:19.080
<i>Did I skip? Did I skip? Did I skip?</i>

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.400
<i>Is that why Abeno-san was mad?!</i>

00:12:22.400 --> 00:12:25.520
Ashiya-dono, you look pale.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:29.760
You should go to the nurse's office, which 
swiftly cures all diseases and injuries.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:32.100
<i>She overestimates our 
school's nurse's office!</i>

00:12:32.920 --> 00:12:34.350
I see.

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:37.880
So the nurse's office can't cure everything.

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:40.080
That was informative.

00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:45.600
But the fact that your school has medical 
facilities is incredible on its own.

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:49.370
This observational visit 
was full of surprises.

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:53.780
Rather than studying a 
single subject all day,

00:12:53.780 --> 00:12:58.250
you divide your time to study a 
variety of subjects in a single day.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:02.460
You also corrected my thinking and 
made me realize that studying

00:13:02.460 --> 00:13:05.900
isn't just sitting at a desk,
but also includes physical activity.

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.260
Your school truly was amazing.

00:13:11.960 --> 00:13:15.080
<i>What Egen-san calls amazing 
sounds natural to me.</i>

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:17.700
<i>But the reason I get to go 
to school like it's normal</i>

00:13:17.700 --> 00:13:22.530
<i>is because of people like Egen-san 
who worked hard to build this system.</i>

00:13:22.940 --> 00:13:25.530
I should study harder.

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.260
Egen-dono, it's time.

00:13:30.880 --> 00:13:32.080
Forgive me.

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:34.040
I got caught up in our conversation.

00:13:34.500 --> 00:13:36.290
See you later, Egen-san.

00:13:41.040 --> 00:13:42.920
See you again.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:50.700
Egen-dono, I'll take you partway there.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:53.310
I appreciate your consideration.

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:55.930
Ashiya, you can leave now.

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:58.230
What? If you're seeing 
her off, I'll go with—

00:13:58.540 --> 00:14:00.320
Abeno-san!

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:06.190
He ignored me again.

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.140
What about Ashiya-dono?

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:24.960
Don't worry about him.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:26.920
I see.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:38.440
Egen-dono, congratulations on 
completing your three-day visit.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:41.680
Thank you for your hospitality.

00:14:41.680 --> 00:14:45.740
Getting permission to visit the mundane 
world this time was no easy feat,

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:47.740
but it was worth the effort.

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:52.100
I couldn't see everything in three days.

00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:56.280
Perhaps you and Ashiya-dono would 
be willing to tell me more about—

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:57.440
Egen-dono.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.300
Yes?

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:00.720
May I ask you something?

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:02.500
Yes, what is it?

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:06.520
How did you acquire permission 
for this observational trip?

00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:09.010
Well... I followed the procedure.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.640
Were you offered a deal?

00:15:12.980 --> 00:15:15.220
In exchange for permission 
to visit the mundane world,

00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.890
were you asked to examine the Mononokean...

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.140
by the Executive?

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.840
In particular, were you 
asked to examine Ashiya?

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:28.150
Um...

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:33.380
Th-There was no deeper meaning to me 
asking Ashiya-dono if he was human!

00:15:33.380 --> 00:15:38.520
The Executive would never ask 
a lowly yokai like myself

00:15:38.520 --> 00:15:42.420
to do something as important 
as examine the Mononokean!

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.660
So you lied about observing to serve 
as a cover for your inspection.

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.050
All that talk about establishing 
a school was a lie, too.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:50.360
That part is true!

00:15:50.360 --> 00:15:52.550
"That part," huh?

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.060
Oh, shoot!

00:15:53.590 --> 00:15:54.760
Like him

00:15:54.060 --> 00:15:55.360
<i>What a terrible liar.</i>

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:58.040
I'm such a fool!

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.640
The Executive will surely scold me...

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:02.260
I wouldn't worry about that.

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:03.060
Huh?

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:08.000
The Executive probably 
expected me to notice.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.570
That bastard.

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:14.760
Oh, and I lied about doubting your 
intentions to observe the school.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:17.100
If I had thought you were 
lying about your request,

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.330
I would've turned you away on the first day.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.300
I see.

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:28.720
You're right. The Executive asked 
me to examine the Mononokean,

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:33.160
but I wasn't forced to in exchange for 
permission to come to the mundane world.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:38.000
The Executive has done much 
to help me build my school.

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:40.700
I accepted his request to repay that debt.

00:16:41.180 --> 00:16:44.840
The Executive did nothing wrong.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:52.460
I must go to the Executive 
to report my observations.

00:16:53.300 --> 00:16:56.900
I must hurry, so you 
needn't come any further.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:01.750
Egen-dono.

00:17:03.780 --> 00:17:07.060
Ashiya doesn't know about the examination.

00:17:07.060 --> 00:17:11.500
He wasn't guarded against you, nor was 
he trying to curry favor with you.

00:17:11.500 --> 00:17:13.760
Simply report exactly 
what you observed today.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:22.560
However, I ask that you tell only 
the Executive that Ashiya is human.

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.940
Give the Executive my regards.

00:17:33.280 --> 00:17:36.300
If he'd alerted me that he knew about 
the examination on the first day,

00:17:36.300 --> 00:17:40.500
I probably wouldn't have accepted
his help for all three.

00:17:42.180 --> 00:17:44.540
Perhaps that's why he didn't say anything.

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.120
All that for me...

00:17:57.120 --> 00:17:57.930
Huh?

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.340
The portal isn't disappearing.

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:01.930
Does that mean...

00:18:01.930 --> 00:18:04.930
Abeno-san is coming back?

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:13.440
I can't just leave now. He's been 
ignoring me since this morning.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:16.040
What are you staring at?

00:18:16.040 --> 00:18:18.480
Since he said that, he's been ignoring me.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:22.320
Even when I talked to him, he wouldn't 
speak, and he kept avoiding me.

00:18:22.320 --> 00:18:26.600
But since I thought he was mad 
at me for staring at Egen-san,

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:29.830
I did my best to talk to him 
even though he was ignoring me.

00:18:30.360 --> 00:18:33.000
Today is the third day of 
my observational visit.

00:18:34.940 --> 00:18:38.800
He didn't tell me we had work last weekend.

00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:42.600
So tired...

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:46.200
You're mad because I didn't go 
to work over the weekend!

00:18:46.200 --> 00:18:46.980
Huh?

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:51.880
But I didn't skip on purpose! 
You didn't tell me we had work!

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:56.040
Besides, if you've got a problem with me, 
you should tell me like you always do!

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:58.900
Just because you're mad, 
you don't have to ignore me!

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.420
Hold on.

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.380
I'm not mad about anything.

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:03.240
What?

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:07.160
And I didn't tell you to 
come to work last weekend.

00:19:07.160 --> 00:19:11.060
Then why did you ignore me all day?

00:19:11.060 --> 00:19:14.540
You wouldn't say a word to me today. 
You were avoiding me, weren't you?

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.250
Stop creeping toward me!

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:18.600
Look, you're avoiding me again!

00:19:18.600 --> 00:19:21.260
Because you're acting like a total weirdo!

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:24.360
What is it? Is it just 
physically impossible?!

00:19:24.360 --> 00:19:27.120
P-Please say something...

00:19:27.120 --> 00:19:30.680
<i>Now that I think about it, I don't 
remember talking to him much today.</i>

00:19:31.200 --> 00:19:33.020
<i>But a whole day?</i>

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:36.880
Wait, could it be that you 
weren't ignoring me,

00:19:38.300 --> 00:19:40.530
but you just weren't talking?

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:44.530
Yeah. Apparently, I guess.

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:47.540
He subconsciously ignored me.

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:47.540
<b>Subconsciously Ignored</b>

00:19:47.540 --> 00:19:51.000
Not only weren't you acting that way because 
you were angry, but it was 0% malicious?

00:19:51.400 --> 00:19:54.340
I was talking to you because
I was desperately trying to raise

00:19:54.340 --> 00:19:57.320
the rapidly dropping excitement 
level since you were ignoring me.

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:00.550
I thought it'd be even more awkward 
if I stopped talking, too.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:05.900
Do you know how much stress I endured 
today because you weren't talking?

00:20:05.900 --> 00:20:08.810
How could you subconsciously ignore me?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:11.810
Are... Are you stupid?!

00:20:19.960 --> 00:20:23.570
Huh? Did I just call Abeno-san...

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:35.600
I can't believe I'd been so 
cautious the past few days.

00:20:35.600 --> 00:20:37.210
I really am an idiot.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:45.160
Click?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.360
Hey, don't lock the door!

00:20:48.360 --> 00:20:50.220
You can call the Mononokean.

00:20:50.220 --> 00:20:50.820
What?!

00:20:50.820 --> 00:20:53.000
And you're not an idiot, Abeno-san.

00:20:53.000 --> 00:20:54.380
See you tomorrow!

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:56.060
Stop playing around! Open the door!

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:57.110
Ashiya!

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.610
He actually left.

00:21:03.560 --> 00:21:06.460
I'll call the Mononokean after a little nap.

00:21:06.460 --> 00:21:10.340
You careless five-year-old. 
You'll pay for this tomorrow.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:15.380
Now that I think about it, it's possible 
it looked like I was ignoring him.

00:21:15.380 --> 00:21:19.220
Since there was a yokai around,
I avoided speaking around humans, too.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:22.460
And then there was the 
business with the Executive.

00:21:40.020 --> 00:21:42.900
He's too careless,

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.530
but I'm too careful.

00:23:25.090 --> 00:23:40.060
<b>Next Time: "The Mortar"</b>

00:23:25.700 --> 00:23:26.840
I'm bored.

00:23:26.840 --> 00:23:30.090
Haruitsuki won't play with me, 
Zenko's gone, and Ashiya...

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:31.260
Well, I don't care about him.

00:23:31.260 --> 00:23:35.350
Darn it! Won't anyone play with me?!

00:23:35.350 --> 00:23:37.390
Next time, "The Mortar."

00:23:37.390 --> 00:23:39.740
Huh? Who are you?
